---
source: crates/deft-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help::common()"
---
Options available on every command:
  -o, --output <value>         Output file or directory; - writes to stdout
  --force                      Overwrite an existing output
  --dry-run                    Show what would happen; write nothing
  --json                       Structured result (or set DEFT_JSON=1)
  -q, --quiet                  No output on success
  -j, --jobs <value>           Parallel jobs (default: CPU cores)
  -r, --recursive              Descend into directories given as input
  --in-place                   Replace the input file (atomically)
  --stdin-format <value>       Format of stdin when it cannot be detected
  --install-engines            Download missing engines (or DEFT_AUTO_INSTALL=1)
  --offline                    Refuse all network access (or DEFT_OFFLINE=1)
  --timeout <value>            Time limit for engine calls, e.g. 5m
  --keep-metadata              Keep original metadata where supported
  -h, --help                   Show help

Inputs: files, globs (expanded by deft), directories, - for stdin.
Outputs never overwrite inputs or existing files unless asked.
Value syntax: deft help values. Error codes: deft help errors.
